WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.310
It's summer already.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.850
A lot has happened since we 
started our love lab in here.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.620
You're revising too much!

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.050
Hell, it turned into pure fantasy 
somewhere in the middle!

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.290
<b>Love Lab?</b>

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.300
A lot has changed since 
we started the love lab,

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.430
but there have been zero 
romantic developments.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.980
We still don't have any contact with boys.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.720
What are you doing, Riko?

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:23.140
My grades are so bad, I've been 
forced to attend cram school.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.040
I've got tons of assignments.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.330
Cram school? The same one that 
the boy you rejected is attending?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.230
What? Really?

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.010
Isn't that awkward?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.300
Don't you have some ex-boyfriends there, too?

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.850
I-It's in the past. It'll be fine!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.260
<i>Plus, it's a lie.</i>

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.930
But they might still like you.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.100
What if they start fighting over Riko-senpai?

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.110
It must be like lying on a bed of nails.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.060
<b>It is right now.</b>

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.700
Is one of your ex-boyfriends...

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.140
that guy?!

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.660
The Yan in your head is 
steadily turning into a monster.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.260
No way.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.500
He did help me out a lot, though.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.370
It was my first time, 
so what he did helped.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.380
It was a little intense for me, though.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.760
What? The Yan inside your
 head's blurred by a mosaic.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.510
Entrance exams were a piece of cake 
for Yan, so I had him help me study.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.950
Oh, the mosaic's gone.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.220
He can be kind, can't he?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.000
<b>Some                                                                Modifications</b>

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.860
I think he said a lifetime's worth of sarcastic 
remarks while we were studying, though.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:33.520
What?

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.520
<b>Editing                                                                              Mistake</b>

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.000
Hey, why don't you investigate the subject 
of this letter while you're at cram school?

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:40.780
Which one?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.370
The one in the suggestion box 
from the south building.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.680
"Hairstyles boys like."

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.200
She's particularly interested in what boys 
from the nearby Southern Middle School think.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.930
The Fuji Girls' Student Council always
 responds to the faith our students put in us.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.170
We must acquire all sorts of information.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.300
And how do you actually feel?

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.780
I'm curious, too.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.440
I'm not sure anyone at my cram school 
is from Southern Middle School.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.220
Besides, everyone's got their own tastes.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.180
But we might find tendencies 
toward a popular preference.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.730
If you can't do that one, then 
ask that boy you rejected about this.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:17.900
What?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.810
What should you say when you just want 
to be friends with someone you're dating?

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.410
I can't ask him that!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.820
Southern Middle School?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.060
He goes there.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.330
Uh, um...

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.720
Sacchan.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.760
Nagi! That's what everyone calls me.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.680
Okay, Nagi-chan!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.890
I'll pound you!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.720
Okay, Nagi-kun.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.990
Why is your reaction even 
worse now, you jerk?!

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.870
Hurry up and say your piece. 
You're getting annoying.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:02.920
What types of girls are popular at your school?

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.450
G-Girls who don't punch boys...

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.940
What hairstyle is the most
 common among the popular girls?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.040
Is there a hairstyle boys from 
Southern Middle School like?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.910
What?

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.320
Everyone's got their own opinion.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.470
I thought as much.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.010
Why are you even asking about that?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.720
Someone I know was asking.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.850
You're always trying to 
help people, aren't you?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.720
Well, I guess silky, long, 
black hair might be popular.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.770
There's apparently a really 
gorgeous girl at Fuji Girls'.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.150
She's the idol of all the boys at our school.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.580
I haven't seen her yet, though.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.760
Do you know her?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.960
<i>Could he mean...</i>

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.330
Southern Middle School's full of scary girls.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.120
We're starved for cute ones.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.030
You're cute.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.380
S-Sorry, I couldn't help it!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.090
But it was a compliment!

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.280
Shut up!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.320
Based on your attitude, I bet you still haven't 
remembered anything about my confession.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.340
Why did I fall for this girl?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.170
Okay.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.070
I just forgot about our past!

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.310
Huh? Wait...

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.730
If you don't remember, 
it's like it never happened.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.260
Ah, what a relief.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.610
My dark past is gone.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.940
<i>"Dark past"?!</i>

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.400
Oh, really?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.530
By the way, there was something 
else I wanted to ask you.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.110
Sure, what is it?

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:34.140
What do you say when you just 
want to be friends with a boy

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.950
who confessed his feelings to you?

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.950
<b>Modified it a little</b>

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.960
Oh? Is something wrong?

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.290
Well...

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.620
Boys will eventually come to their 
senses and leave inconsiderate girls

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.890
who don't consider boys' feelings,

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:49.630
so I'd say just ride it out.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.840
I see.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.630
What?

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.350
Straight, black hair is popular?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.590
Not fluffy cotton candy, 
but silky, pitch black hair?

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:10.700
<i>The idol Nagi mentioned is probably Maki.</i>

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.450
Boys will eventually come to their 
senses and leave inconsiderate girls.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.570
What... Riko?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.480
Why are you curling my hair?

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:29.080
You said you wanted to 
change your hairstyle before.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.720
Stop!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.620
<b>Maki's House</b>

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.060
If straight, black hair is popular,

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.900
we should develop a plan to 
make the most of this weapon,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.060
and tell the girl who submitted the request.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.640
I must work harder to care for my hair!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.570
It's time for a bath.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:53.380
All your pain will disappear.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:56.700
Cold is the enemy of girls and your liver.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.410
Natsuo, let me borrow a book.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.250
Huh? Is she in the bath?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.710
Ah, she must have been studying.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.070
Let's see...

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:12.580
Operation: Hair Appeal

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.010
"Operation: Hair Appeal"?

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:20.180
Maki Natsuo's "Operation: Hair Appeal," Part 1!

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.180
Place a large fan in front of 
Southern Middle School's gate.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.860
Show off your fluttering hair, 
and become popular.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.310
I'm not sure I can use the 
budget to pay for a large fan...

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.640
I know!

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.740
If a typhoon comes, you can become 
popular without spending a thing!

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.850
Operation Part 2!

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:42.940
Wet your hair for a sexy look.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.450
It's not unnatural during pool season.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.130
It's a ten-minute walk from Fuji Girls' 
to Southern Middle School.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.800
Considering the time it takes to dry,

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.370
if you leave dripping wet, it will be
 perfect by the time you get there.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.380
Sparkling drops in your hair 
will multiply the effect.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:00.210
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.230
Rejected.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.220
Why?!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:15.900
Maki Natsuo's "Operation: 
Hair Appeal (Modified)," Part 1!

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.580
Dance near the school!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.040
Part 2!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.970
Play in a band near the school!

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.310
Part 3!

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.160
Fish near the school!

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.600
Part 4!

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:28.920
Cram school?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.520
Your tutor Matsubara-san is quitting 
after she gets married, right?

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.720
The cram school my acquaintance 
runs is supposed to be quite good.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:39.180
But you said I couldn't go to cram 
school because there are boys there.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:44.310
Father, something is wrong with Natsuo!

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.120
What's wrong?

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.950
Perhaps because of her 
lack of contact with boys,

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:52.590
her aspiration for romance 
has grown increasingly wild.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.500
If she meets a smooth-talking boy, 
she'll fall for his lines in a heartbeat.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.450
Your overprotective nature is also to blame!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.700
What?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.690
You need to let Natsuo learn 
something about reality!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.080
You shouldn't have any contact 
with boys at your girls' school either...

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.070
<b>Currently attending 
Fujisaki Girls' Academy</b>

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.120
You sound like you know 
something about the real world.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.120
I'm shocked.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.880
The advanced classes seem quite 
difficult, so I won't force you—

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:18.960
I'll go! I'll go!

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.360
It's time to show the fruits of my labor.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.480
I'm talking about academics, of course!

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.480
Oh, really?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.050
<b>Now knows the truth</b>

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.650
<i>Now I'll finally have contact with boys, too.</i>

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.540
<i>I might finally meet the prince of my dreams.</i>

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.960
Natsuo, we're here.

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:38.650
Yes, Father.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.100
Masaomi-san.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:50.710
The girl joining the advanced 
class is going to be visiting today.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:54.380
Irikimi-sensei, could you 
call me by my family name?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.290
I'm calling you Masaomi out of friendliness.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:00.040
It actually feels strangely distant.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.370
Maybe I'll call you Yan-san, like Riko-san does.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:04.900
Masaomi is fine.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.980
So, I hope you'll be nice to the new girl.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.210
I hope she doesn't quit immediately, 
saying she can't keep up.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.440
Two people just quit recently.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.670
Don't worry. She's a smart girl.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.640
Oh, she's here.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.910
This is your new friend, Maki-san.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:32.770
I need to speak with her father. 
Will you show her around?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.590
This way.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.300
Just the two of them?

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.490
This isn't what we agreed upon.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.540
They just quit the other day.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:41.590
There will be more soon.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.550
<i>He could've told me her family name.</i>

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.780
What's your name?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.110
<i>The teacher just said my family name.</i>

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.100
It's Natsuo.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.090
<i>Natsuo. Natsuo Maki, huh?</i>

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.650
Well, Natsuo-san.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.060
<b>Natsuo-san</b>

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:02.660
Y-You can't call me that!

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:03.510
What?

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.240
Wh-What are you... A-And honorifics... D-Don't...

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:09.750
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.480
<i>She doesn't want me to use honorifics?</i>

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.540
So... Natsuo, then?

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.910
<b>Natsuo</b>

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.180
I don't have my IC recorder!

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.260
No, that's not the problem!

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:23.880
I must have misheard him...

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.590
Are you all right, Natsuo?

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.810
Riko!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.730
Riko!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.890
She's gorgeous!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.980
Drop-dead gorgeous!

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.650
M-Maki?!

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.050
Riko!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.320
Wh-What's wrong? Calm down.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.810
What are you doing here, anyway?

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:49.350
There you are.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.280
Why did you suddenly start shouting...

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.620
Yan-san stole another one of my firsts!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.750
N-No, I didn't!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.550
What's all this ruckus?

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.650
G-Gosh, I've created such a mess.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:08.800
I'm sorry for causing so much trouble.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:14.480
If I were as popular as Riko, I wouldn't 
get upset over something like this.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:15.850
I'm ashamed.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.060
Popular?

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:21.180
You know, don't you?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.190
She's always been...

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.190
Hey, let's go.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.480
I'll see you at school tomorrow.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.780
Popular?

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:34.250
Have you been putting on 
airs to fool your friends?

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.680
N-No, you idiot!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.020
You don't know anything.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.570
I feel terrible now!

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.010
Yeah, I do...

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.340
<i>I feel terrible.</i>

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:54.050
<b>The one who feels
 the most terrible</b>

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.500
<i>That's me.</i>

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.060
Riko.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.120
Maki.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.460
Did you hear?

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.740
The school's policy changed

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.480
from forbidding romantic 
relationships, to encouraging them.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.150
What?!

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:10.470
We don't have to conduct our 
love lab in secret anymore!

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:12.120
Let's begin conducting

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.620
Love Master Riko's romantic technique 
courses at all school meetings!

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.610
Wait, I can't do that!

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:19.580
Why not?

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:23.590
Because you've been putting on airs to fool 
your friends into thinking you're popular?

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.800
N-No, there's a reason for this!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:31.150
Let's hear it after school 
in the faculty office, then.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:32.910
For now, you can stand.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:33.600
What?!

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.460
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.470
You're slacking off.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.260
You're a member of the 
student council, aren't you?

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:39.810
Pull yourself together.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.180
Come on, tie your necktie.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.900
Your president, Maki, 
always looks so sharp.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.660
<i>Maki's perfect, but when she's here...</i>

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:54.810
Hey.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.070
What's wrong, Maki?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.590
Goodbye, pure girl memory.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:06.520
Are you talking about what 
happened at cram school yesterday?

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.590
When you said Yan stole 
another of your firsts?

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.340
Yes. He's far too cruel.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.310
He took it from me.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.270
T-Took what?

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:21.400
The memory of my first time being
 called Natsuo without an honorific!

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:24.940
He suddenly said my name without an honorific!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.230
Twice, even!

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:29.280
<i>Has Yan always been that kind of guy?</i>

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.110
Come on, that's nothing.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.030
Nothing?

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.650
I know you don't understand how 
someone inexperienced in love feels,

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:40.670
given how popular and 
experienced you are, but still!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.320
Understands 
completely

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.500
I'm sure it's nothing to make a fuss over,

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.250
but I had always longed 
to be called by my name.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.340
I even imagined an ideal situation.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:16:04.970
<b>Days  Hours  Minutes  Seconds</b>

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.980
My boyfriend still hasn't 
called me by my name.

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:59.380
Since we began dating, it's been
 86 days, 9 hours, 27 minutes, and 3,

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:02.150
4, 5, 6...

00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:04.890
That's a terrifying sentimental countdown!

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.820
The sunny weather turns into a hurricane.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.240
Go home.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.320
Just like my heart.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.990
That's way too wild.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:15.430
<b>Ramen</b>

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:13.880
A sign comes flying by.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.540
Seriously, go home!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.430
<i>Watch out, Natsuo!</i>

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:18.700
Did you just call me Natsuo?

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.400
That's a ridiculous development.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.260
Say it again.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:23.370
<i>Later.</i>

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.330
Go home already!

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.240
But, he said it so easily...

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:32.360
What's important is having 
someone you love say it.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.720
So don't worry about it.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.310
You're right.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:40.560
That boy you rejected never uses honorifics
 with you, but it doesn't bother you.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.320
I feel much better.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.520
Thank you, Riko.

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:49.360
Have you been putting on 
airs to fool your friends?

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.870
I feel worse.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.760
Wh-What's wrong?

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.310
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:02.200
It's President Maki!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.000
She's always so neat and trim.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:06.420
Her fluttering hair is so beautiful.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:09.150
But there's no wind right now.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:13.610
Princess Fuji is so beautiful, she 
even controls natural phenomena!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.380
Such feminine strength!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.880
<b>Superhuman 
Strength</b>

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.680
Are you a master of love?

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:28.350
W-Well, yeah! I've had a 
few boyfriends, of course.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.610
<i>Why did I say that?</i>

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.610
<i>If I hadn't said that, this 
never would have happened.</i>

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.620
Shut up!

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.920
Oh? Are you in a bad mood?

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:44.330
Did something happen?

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.330
Huh? Oh... no, nothing.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.250
How was that, then?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:52.700
I was performing "Beautiful 
Hair Fluttering in the Wind."

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.510
I thought you were broiling eels.

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:57.850
The wind doesn't always blow.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.340
With your own wind, you'll 
never miss an opportunity.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.970
You can fan yourself from 
the shadows, like this.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.890
That's terrifying!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.280
At least use a portable fan.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.420
But producing results the easy 
way doesn't seem satisfying.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.590
It's all right. You'll never produce results.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.820
Shadows are dark and scary, aren't they?

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.950
I'm not sure you understand what's scary.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.620
I know.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.530
I can use the light, and...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.850
It's so hot today.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.780
The hallways are boiling.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:34.490
Oh, my.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:36.880
Was I so stunning, I made your jaws drop?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.900
Increasing the beauty of your 
hair with the power of light,

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.690
"Operation: Backlit Goddess."

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:42.920
An evil goddess!

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:45.480
Its appeal seems almost devilish, doesn't it?

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.350
You optimistic devil.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.820
Hey! The eco goddess who 
needs no air conditioner!

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:50.770
Don't encourage her!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.010
I suddenly feel a chill.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.360
A performance of fluttering hair?

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.980
What are you, stupid?

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.410
You're always coming up with such lame ideas.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.290
You've got it wrong! That's just a habit!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:10.460
Fanning yourself is fine as 
long as you don't overdo it.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.170
Just do it normally.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.670
I-I see.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:17.570
They're rather bulky to carry around, though.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:20.260
That's where the portable slapstick comes in!

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.300
Why a slapstick?

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:24.270
You can slap people <i>and </i>fan yourself!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:25.930
This picture doesn't make sense!

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:30.300
They'll know you're a girl who will come back 
with sharp remarks when people act stupid!

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:33.440
Why are you always so confident 
when it comes to slapsticks?

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:38.110
When I went to public school, 
we used desk pads as fans.

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:40.010
So did I.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.580
I would fan myself under my clothes.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.240
I played with static electricity.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:44.860
I threw mine!

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:52.750
Huggy!

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.420
This is it!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.340
What is?

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.480
Break out your desk pad in front of 
Southern Middle School and fan yourself!

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.300
It's natural.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.320
Not at all.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.410
It's a little embarrassing, but you 
can fan yourself under your clothes.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.740
You'll be fanning the flames.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.110
You think that's pretty clever, don't you?

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:13.520
Direct attention to your hair by 
playing with static electricity.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.090
Show off your innocence.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.350
You can single out boys around you, too.

00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:19.560
That seems awfully malicious.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:22.140
Then, throw it at the boy you like.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.540
It'll create an opportunity to speak with him.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:25.320
You have a full course for that desk pad?

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.370
There. We have our answer.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.430
As our representative of 
straight, long, black hair,

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:36.200
I will instruct you in techniques for 
effectively showing off your hair.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.050
You better not be talking 
about using a desk pad.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:43.220
But, if we respond to this one, I feel 
like we'll receive even more requests.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.230
We'll never run out of 
subjects for our love lab.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:47.640
That's nothing to be happy about.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.960
We're about to get even busier.

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.600
What are you going to do if you push 
yourself too hard and collapse again?

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.900
You're right. We can't respond to all of them.

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.040
After all we've dealt with recently,

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.230
I'd like to avoid drawing attention for a while.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.570
But we can't ignore them.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.120
Maybe we could just pick 
up the ones that seem easy.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.090
If the student council chooses, 
it may make some students bitter.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:11.010
They may think we're playing favorites.

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:12.700
This is so annoying.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.620
Why don't you tell them using this?

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.470
Hey, yeah, the newspaper association...

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:19.460
What?

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.060
Well, they...

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:31.290
We thought we heard someone 
calling, so we came running.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:32.470
Liar!

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:34.640
We brought our newest paper.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.980
We're proud of this one.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.680
<b>Fuji Girls' News (Trial Copy)</b>

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.680
Friends are great!

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.680
<b><b>Friendship and Smiles</b></b>

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.680
<b>A Rare Shot of Mizushima Sayori's Smile</b>

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.440
You're so mean.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.330
We printed on both sides for this one.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:45.600
<b>Princess Boom</b>
 in the Student Council?

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:44.680
<b>A Mysterious Princess (LOL) Appears!</b>

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.660
Nice paper.

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:50.980
Don't react like that!

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.880
It really is a nice paper.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.250
Don't react like that, either!

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:56.920
Aren't Nana-chan's photos wonderful?

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.880
I'm not sure they're as good 
as your writing, Momo-senpai.

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:03.390
Ichikawa-senpai, your photos are wonderful.

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:04.300
I knew you could do it.

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:06.630
Y-You think so?

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:08.940
It really is a nice paper.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:10.760
Nice and harsh.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:11.760
So funny...

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:13.260
Isn't it?

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:15.540
But what we'd like you to focus on is...

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.060
Under the main article.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:17.690
Right here.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:27.060
<b>Love Lab Correspondence</b>

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:21.620
Romance Lab Correspondence?

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:23.770
Call it the Love Lab Correspondence.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:24:03.320
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:00.870
<i>Maki's being pushed around.</i>

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:02.790
<i>It's kind of refreshing, though.</i>

00:24:02.990 --> 00:24:05.060
<i>Don't act unconcerned 
because it doesn't affect you.</i>

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:10.270
<i>Letting my hair flutter while I'm being 
pushed around seems romantically effective.</i>

00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:12.400
<i>Do you want someone to grab 
your legs and spin you around?</i>

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:15.760
<i>That's just a giant swing. What 
are you, a professional wrestler?</i>

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:18.320
<i>Love truly is war.</i>

00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:19.930
<i>How deep.</i>

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:22.100
<i>Love isn't scripted, though.</i>

00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:27.140
<b>Be My Friend Forever</b>

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:24.590
<i>Don't say such dangerous things!</i>

00:24:27.170 --> 00:24:30.100
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
